WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.804
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Wednesday, November eighteenth.

2
00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:13.920
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.788
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.788 --> 00:00:28.288
Today: Iran launches drones at Kuwait and Bahrain, a national strike called in Colombia for tomorrow, new Ebola figures and travel measures, a polio detection in Syria, and Iranian security forces deployed to major cities.

5
00:00:28.288 --> 00:00:29.672
We start in the Gulf.

6
00:00:29.672 --> 00:00:41.866
Kuwait's armed forces said overnight that their air defenses were engaging drone threats, and urged the public to stay calm and follow official safety instructions, according to the Kuwait News Agency.

7
00:00:41.866 --> 00:00:50.278
Al Jazeera, citing Iranian state media, reports Iran's army said it targeted U.S. drone and missile installations at Ali Al Salem Air Base in Kuwait.

8
00:00:50.278 --> 00:00:59.973
In Bahrain, the Bahrain Defence Force said its air defenses intercepted several Iranian aerial attacks early today, Reuters and the Kuwait News Agency report.

9
00:00:59.973 --> 00:01:10.291
Al Jazeera reports the U.S. struck an Iranian missile site on Qeshm Island in the Strait of Hormuz, and that six oil tankers have reportedly been damaged by sea mines in the strait.

10
00:01:10.291 --> 00:01:14.470
Saudi Arabia also condemned an attack on a U.A.E. oil tanker, Al Arabiya reports.

11
00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:20.783
Kuwait's Foreign Ministry condemned the repeated Iranian attacks on its territory.

12
00:01:20.783 --> 00:01:22.362
Next, Colombia.

13
00:01:22.362 --> 00:01:36.444
The State Department says labor unions, social organizations and opposition groups have called a national strike and demonstrations for this Thursday, November nineteenth, in Bogotá, Medellín, Cali, Barranquilla and Bucaramanga, with more gatherings and marches possible in other cities.

14
00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:41.706
An update on the Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo.

15
00:01:41.706 --> 00:01:49.124
The U.N. humanitarian office says more than eleven thousand four hundred cases have been reported, and nearly half of those infected have died.

16
00:01:49.124 --> 00:01:57.029
Reuters reports the U.N. says insecurity is complicating efforts to contain the outbreak.

17
00:01:57.029 --> 00:02:09.917
Separately, Australia's Smartraveller says El Salvador now requires a twenty one day quarantine for health monitoring for travelers who visited or transited parts of Central or East Africa in the twenty one days before arrival.

18
00:02:09.917 --> 00:02:22.001
In Syria, the World Health Organization says circulating variant poliovirus type one has been detected in Deir ez Zor governorate, and the health ministry, backed by the W H O and UNICEF, is scaling up vaccination and surveillance.

19
00:02:22.001 --> 00:02:34.157
And in Iran, the Institute for the Study of War and Critical Threats assess that the regime has likely deployed security forces to some major Iranian cities in recent days, as part of preparations for potential anti regime protests.

20
00:02:34.157 --> 00:02:37.879
Now a few quick notes by region.

21
00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:46.513
In the Middle East, Reuters reports the Houthis say they launched drones toward Saudi Arabia's East West pipeline.

22
00:02:46.513 --> 00:02:53.160
The Kuwait News Agency reports the Saudi led coalition said it intercepted a Houthi cruise missile fired toward Riyadh.

23
00:02:53.160 --> 00:03:00.062
And Reuters reports Houthi run Al Masirah TV showed a factory in Hodeidah on fire after reported Saudi strikes.

24
00:03:00.062 --> 00:03:04.086
In Europe, an update on Ukraine's strikes on the bridge to Crimea.

25
00:03:04.086 --> 00:03:14.121
The Institute for the Study of War says Ukrainian forces struck the Kerch Strait Bridge for a second straight night, completely collapsing its road sections and damaging the railway section.

26
00:03:14.121 --> 00:03:22.254
Reuters reports hoax bomb threats have hit more than eight thousand institutions across Europe over the past month, rattling schools and airports.

27
00:03:22.254 --> 00:03:23.113
And the U.S.

28
00:03:23.113 --> 00:03:29.372
Geological Survey reports a preliminary magnitude five point three earthquake in Romania.

29
00:03:29.372 --> 00:03:32.326
In Africa, an update on the Ethiopia and Eritrea border.

30
00:03:32.326 --> 00:03:39.802
ACLED says Eritrean forces regained control of Badme over the weekend and advanced about twenty kilometers toward Tigray.

31
00:03:39.802 --> 00:03:47.952
Al Jazeera, drawing on ACLED data, reports renewed clashes between Somali police and Oromo militias in Moyale, Ethiopia, have displaced thousands.

32
00:03:47.952 --> 00:04:00.505
In the Americas, the State Department says farmers are blocking highways at five locations in Jalisco outside Guadalajara, Mexico, to protest a lack of government support for agriculture.

33
00:04:00.505 --> 00:04:01.919
That's today's brief.

34
00:04:01.919 --> 00:04:10.409
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

35
00:04:10.409 --> 00:04:18.745
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

36
00:04:18.745 --> 00:04:20.884
This brief is digitally narrated.

37
00:04:20.884 --> 00:04:21.844
Questions?

38
00:04:21.844 --> 00:04:25.476
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

39
00:04:25.476 --> 00:04:27.601
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
